{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773423503,"nonce":"DToZvCr0KVR8zoWDs3J4Q6L7H0o=","title":"Race: watcher cleanup removes session dir under running container","message":"## Problem\n\nWhen a git-bug issue is closed while a container is running, the watcher removes the session dir and worktree. The running container then crashes with FileNotFoundError because /session/ was unmounted from under it.\n\nObserved in jessica-ng review container (ec756ccd4683):\n```\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '/session/raw-output.log'\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`session_monitor.check_closed_issues()` cleans up sessions for closed issues without checking if the container is still running. The cleanup races with the container's file I/O.\n\n## Fix\n\nBefore cleaning up a session, check `docker_container_status(container_name)`. If the container is running, stop it first (or skip cleanup until it exits). The container name is derivable from the session ID.\n\n## Requirement\n\nREQ-002 (Session lifecycle management)","files":null}]}